    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just a theory to me though, i can feel it in my bones. the skepticism is exactly the problem... people always dismiss what they cant understand. i've been looking at the ways my ancestors always seemed to occupy these specific roles in history, like they were observing rather than participating. it makes so much sense now. if i'm supposed to be preparing for the mars transition, how do i start commanding respect in my daily life? i feel like i'm wearing a mask of being 'normal' and it's exhausting. how do i carry myself so people see the authority i actually have?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
